<title>JAPAN: S.Korea's KDB launches 5.1% yen/dlr samurai -- Daiwa.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's KDB launches 5.1% yen/dlr samurai -- Daiwa.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following yen/dollar dual currency samurai bond issue was announced by lead manager Daiwa Securities on Monday:</p>
<p> BORROWER	  Korea Development Bank (KDB)</p>
<p> AMT		 30 bln yen</p>
<p> COUPON	    5.1 pct</p>
<p> MATURITY	  21 Aug 2000</p>
<p> ISS PRICE	 par</p>
<p> PAY DATE	  21 Feb 1997</p>
<p> SUB PERIOD	Jan 29 to Feb 20</p>
<p> PAY FREQ	  Annual</p>
<p> LAST RATING     S&amp;P AA-, Moody's A1, JBRI AA+</p>
<p> LEAD MANAGER    Daiwa Securities</p>
<p> LEAD TRUSTEE    Long-Term Credit Bank of Japan</p>
<p>NOTE: Holders of the samurai bonds will receive $4,255.32 for each 500,000-yen bond held at maturity.</p>
</text>
